1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
If you lose to me,

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
I'll take your left arm.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Well, not to be rude,
but instead of my left arm,

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
do you think that it'd be okay
if just bet the same thing

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Usually?

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,000
And what is that?

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
I bet my life.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Your life, huh?

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
I'm just beginning to realize
it was I who lacked resolve.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
[opening theme music playing]

11
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
[singer singing in English]

12
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

13
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
KNOV X AND X MOREL

14
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
-[thunder rumbling]
-[rain pattering]

15
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
while Knov uses this opportunity
to infiltrate the palace.

16
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
[thunder rumbling]

17
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
[Knov panting]

18
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Finally, I made it.

19
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The stairs are still
over a hundred meters away.

20
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Giant fruit on bizarre trees,

21
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
About 500 on each one…

22
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,000
And 10 trees totals 5,000.

23
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
But after only one day,

24
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Killua's interference
brought the process to a grinding halt,

25
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
so it adds up.

26
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
These cocoons hold the selected humans.

27
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Neferpitou is probably a Manipulator,

28
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:50,000
and, if so, almost certainly intends
to manipulate these soldiers

29
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,000
into invading the rest of the world
as per the King's will.

30
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,000
The palace entrance looks dark.
No one's there.

31
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
So far, so good.

32
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Middle exit. Set.

33
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Now for the near exit.

34
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
I don't see any guards anywhere.

35
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
I'd wager that there's only
a select few waiting inside.

36
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,000
KING

37
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
We must delay any reinforcements,
even if only for a second.

38
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
CENTRAL STAIRCASE

39
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
The first floor is too far.

40
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,000
The central stairway, second floor,
that's the best location.

41
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
The central staircase
is beyond this courtyard.

42
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Should I make one here, just in case?

43
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
No, that would be no different
from the one outside.

44
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,000
I have to at least get close
to the first floor's central staircase,

45
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
preferably up the stairs
on the second floor.

46
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Hmm? [gasps]

47
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,000
[Knov] Scream.

48
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
[Nen whooshing]

49
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Are there any others around?

50
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
If they saw me, it's over.

51
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
[panting]

52
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
I'll have to retreat.

53
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
[sighs]

54
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,000
So it was alone.

55
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
[gasps]

56
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
It's like it's full of
everything sinister in the world.

57
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,000
It's not that I fear death, not anymore.

58
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
What I fear most

59
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,000
is that the ones lurking up there
would go to great lengths

60
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:46,000
to wring out any info I have on the King
before killing me,

61
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
which they would do
in the cruelest way they could think of.

62
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
If I'm caught, I won't be able to resist.

63
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
[exhales]

64
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
[rain pattering]

65
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Huh?

66
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:38,000
You look familiar.
Aren't you that lion guy I saw on TV?

67
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:42,000
My name is Leol, and don't you forget it.

68
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:46,000
I was told that I should expect
to meet up with a wolf and a lobster.

69
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:50,000
I'm afraid that those two are busy
dealing with the grunts you created,

70
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,000
which means I can fight you one-on-one.

71
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,000
I do appreciate the personal attention.

72
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
This guy's just as strong as Cheetu.

73
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
No, he's a little stronger.

74
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Now, let's get started.

75
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:09,000
[Morel] Allowing Knov
to get into the palace is my top priority.

76
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
I need to focus on
keeping the enemy's attention.

77
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[growls] That's not gonna help.

78
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,000
there are also women inside.

79
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Not for the King

80
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:53,000
but for the lecherous
Director Bizeff himself.

81
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:57,000
If our strategy worked,
Palm is among them.

82
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
You can leave the fourth truck
right there.

83
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
[Marcos] Yes, sir.

84
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,000
And, now, if you would please excuse us.

85
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Hmm.

86
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,000
[chuckles]

87
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
[whistling a tune]

88
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
[whistling continues]

89
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
[slurps]

90
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
[engine turns off]

91
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,000
[chuckles]

92
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[chuckles]

93
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
You have but one job while you're here,

94
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,000
and that is to carry out all of my orders.

95
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,000
When you are summoned,

96
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,000
you must drop everything
and come to see me at once.

97
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
[women] Yes, Director, sir.

98
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,000
[Bizeff] Excellent.

99
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
-You there.
-[gasps]

100
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
And, as for the rest of you ladies,
you can go wait in your rooms.

101
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
[women] Right.

102
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,000
We made the cut. We made it.

103
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Oh, we must have caught his fancy.

104
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,000
[both laughing]

105
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
[Palm] I have to find a way out of here.

106
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,000
I must see the King
and his Royal Guards myself.

107
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:44,000
[narrator] Once Palm has seen a person
up close and with her own eyes,

108
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,000
[panting]

109
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
[shivering]

110
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,000
that… that vicious Aura…

111
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
[crying] One glance

112
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,000
You may have even touched it.

113
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
[sobbing]

114
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,000
How could you still face them?

115
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,000
How?

116
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
Palm! [sobbing]

117
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Please, don't push your luck.

118
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Please, I'm begging you.

119
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Hmm?

120
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:28,000
It's almost too perfect
that, after all that running,

121
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:40,000
the perfect location
for your painfully violent death.

122
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Sorry, but you'll have to say
your own prayers.

123
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
You see, I'm an atheist.

124
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,000
[chuckles]
That's pretty optimistic of you.

125
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Now, let's see which of us
is really cornered.

126
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,000
[exhales]

127
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Hmm?

128
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
[grunts]

129
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:19,000
[Morel] So he led me here
knowing full well?

130
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:22,000
[chuckles] Works for me.

131
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:25,000
If he believes
that everything is going his way,

132
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
he won't hesitate
to put his own abilities on display.

133
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,000
But I've seen some flexible abilities
in my time,

134
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:37,000
and not a single one of them
could hold a candle to my Deep Purple.

135
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
I feel tingly.

136
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:47,000
I love it, the moment
an opponent showcases their abilities.

137
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,000
It's addictive.

138
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Still, it might make more sense to attack
before he reveals what he can do.

139
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:00,000
But no, that's not how a man fights.

140
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:20,000
Check out their second album.
That one is the coolest.

141
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,000
The 12 songs on it form a story,

142
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:39,000
is that the album's
exactly 60 minutes long.

143
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,000
It's a classic.

144
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Yeah. I hate to say it, but you're right.

145
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,000
[Morel] This is bad.

146
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,000
[closing theme song playing]

147
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[upbeat music playing]

148
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[Gon] Next time, Return and Retire.

149
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,000
Killua! Killua!

150
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
[Killua] Return on! To the preview!

151
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
[Gon crying] It has to be you, Killua!

152
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,000
[Killua] Hey, stop crying.

153
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:45,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
